title: Change order form for bathroom remodels (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable change-order form for bathroom remodels. Fixtures, tile area, plumbing and electrical moves, allowances, hidden damage, the new total and both signatures. No account needed.
heading: Change order for bathrooms
sub: For when the customer picks a different tub, or you open a wall and find rot. Fill it in and get both signatures before the extra work starts.
tips:
  - If you find hidden damage, take photos and write what you found and where before you fix it.
  - For an allowance item, write the allowance and what the customer's pick actually costs. The difference goes in the price change.
  - Moving plumbing or electrical can mean a permit or another inspection. Write down who gets it.
  - Both sides sign and date it before the extra work starts. Give the customer a copy.
  - Some states have their own rules for change orders. Check with your state licensing board.
---
